<title>GERMANY: Germany meets only two EMU criteria - paper.</title>
<headline>Germany meets only two EMU criteria - paper.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany at present fulfils only two of the criteria required to qualify for European monetary union, Bild newspaper reported on Wednesday, citing a finance ministry report on convergence to be presented to the cabinet.</p>
<p>Bild said that of all 15 European Union countries only Luxembourg met the four key criteria on inflation, the budget deficit, public debt and interest rates.</p>
<p>Three states -- Denmark, France and the Netherlands -- met three of the criteria and seven states -- Belgium, Germany, Finland, Britain, Ireland, Austria and Sweden -- met two of the requirements, Bild reported.</p>
<p>Four states met none of the criteria -- Greece, Italy, Portugal and Spain, the report said.</p>
<p>Countries will be judged on their economic performance in 1997 whether they qualify for membership of the single currency, due to be launched on January 1, 1999.</p>
